---
description: Prefer referencing HTTP types via the crate-root
alwaysApply: true
---

Use `http::Type` paths (not `crate::http::Type`)

- Prefer referencing HTTP types via the crate-root re-export `http::...` in public-facing code, examples, and tests.
- Rationale: mirrors user code, improves readability, and matches Axum-style docs.
- Examples:
  - Good: `http::Method`, `http::Request`, `http::HeaderMap`
  - Bad: `crate::http::Method`, `crate::http::Request`, `crate::http::HeaderMap`

